The first proof closes, but I’m tightening artifact traceability before calling it done: the claims will reference a generated K constant built from `solution.mpy`. That way, changing the Python implementation changes the theorem being proved (and an incorrect mutation makes compilation or proof fail), instead of leaving a stale hard-coded AST in `spec.k`.
